From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Check for SSE to define __intXX_t

The UnionM128 members are declared with the __intXX_t types, which are
glibc reserved names from bits/types.h rather than standard ones, so on C
libraries that do not happen to define them, musl among them, every SSE2
build fails. Define them next to the emscripten ones, which is a no-op
where they already exist, since they are typedefs of the same types.

This is the PhysX 4.1 patch of the same name, forward ported to 5.9.0.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/unix/sse2/PxUnixSse2AoS.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/unix/sse2/PxUnixSse2AoS.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/unix/sse2/PxUnixSse2AoS.h
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/unix/sse2/PxUnixSse2AoS.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/unix/sse2/PxUnixSse2AoS.h
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ namespace physx
 namespace aos
 {
 
-#if PX_EMSCRIPTEN
+#if PX_EMSCRIPTEN || PX_SSE2
 typedef int8_t   __int8_t;
 typedef int16_t  __int16_t;
 typedef int32_t  __int32_t;
